Z||000000||lowfunds||03-26-2001||01:37 PM||||I am pulling a 97 3800sc this weekend. I need to know exactly what I need from the grand prix. I will be getting the engine, trans, computor, harness, fuel pump, anything else anyone can think of? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||gabriel||03-26-2001||01:47 PM||||Get the purge canister & the air filter box. The exhaust pipe might be good to get.<BR>I didn't know that you could use that fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowfunds||03-26-2001||01:55 PM||||Im not sure if I can but I thought terryk said it could be used with some modification.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||03-26-2001||03:03 PM||||Get:<P>1. Get the plastic fuel lines that connect to the fuel rail. At least get the quick disconnect connectors. You can peel the line from the connectors and reuse them.<P>2. The pipe from the rear manifold to the cat (downpipe).<P>3. Purge canister and hoses.<P>4. A set of A-body trans bracket from any 3800/440/4T60/4T60E A-body car. The cradle mod's depend on the year of the Fiero. I used A-body rubber mounts. You will need C Wests 3800 engine bracket but use the A-body rubber mount. Order early so you get it within a month.<P>5. If using the 4T65E, get a set of 94/up 3800 A-body axles or 92/up 3800 U van axles. These used the 4T60E. These are the correct length. The 440 or 4T60 (non-E) are wrong length. Well, the driver's side is correct but the passenger side is wrong (too long). You can always buy the correct shaft from GM for about $35. I have the PN.<P>6. Get the AC hose if you can. You will need it for the custom AC hose.<P>7. The air box won't fit, but at least get the hose from the box to the TB. You can use the IAT from the Fiero.<P>8. The fuel pump *may* be a tight squeeze through the Fiero tank hole. GM used two sizes (physically). If so, buy an 89 Turbo Trans Am fuel pump. Napa has them for around $50. God help you, make sure the pump is isolated from the metal lines or you will hear the pump screaming in the passenger compartment. <P>Can't think of anything else right now.   <P>Throttle cable, oil filter adapter (the GTP adpater may hit the engine bracket) coolant lines, heater hoses, shifter lever (works backwards and doesn't have the necessary range to select PRND321), exhaust, etc. all need attention and changing. <P>If this SC has the large aluminum AC compressor mount, consider getting an A-body steel mount. My AL bracket hits the cradle on decel (very close) and I think the steel bracket doesn't come down as far. I was planning on switching them.<P>For the upper dogbone mount, an A-body engine bracket will work. You will need to make a mount on the trunk.<P>I'll look at my GTP and see what else pops into mind.<P>Two questions:<P>Are you in an emissions test area? Can you switch the 4T65E for a 4T60E for the same cost?<P>TK<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowfunds||03-26-2001||08:40 PM||||TK  NO and probbly not I will check tommarow,but they have the complete car and I don't think they have another trans, anything else come to mind? thanks for the info... also you have mail.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-27-2001||02:00 AM||||I sent you my phone number. Give me a call. The 65E is a nice trans. MAKE SURE YOU GET THE KEY AND LOCK CYLINDER FROM THE STEERING COLUMN........That pesky Passkey II.||||reg||1
